From a2c0d5cfe4cf436624f48693536f0f365e4572ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:41:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/46] vulkan: flat grouped-query fold for few-token flash
 attention (speculative verify at depth)

The decode GQA fold runs one coopmat1 workgroup per query token (gqa_ratio rows of a 16-row tile), so a verify
batch of N tokens reads K/V N times and fills 6 of 16 rows for 24/4 heads. For 2..8 tokens the coopmat1 row
tiles now run over the flattened (token, query head) rows of one KV head (GQA_FLAT_BIT): row R -> token
R / gqa_ratio, head R % gqa_ratio, per-row Q / mask / output addressing. Exact (same per-row math; split counts
change, so the last bits can differ). Knob GGML_VK_FA_GQA_FLAT=0 (off) / <n> (max tokens, default 8).

Qwen3.8-27B (24/4 heads, hd 256, f16 cache) on Radeon 8060S, KV 32K, in the model: 16 FA calls of an 8-token
DFlash2 verify 42.9 -> 17.7 ms, 5-token MTP verify 23.9 -> 13.0 ms. test-backend-ops: verify-shape eval and
perf cases (2..16 tokens, cache layout, q8_0, sinks, ALiBi, other GQA ratios).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
